  'Medical-Surgical Nursing II',
  'Medical-Surgical Nursing II',
  'This course extends adult medical-surgical nursing into advanced acute-care and complex patient management. Students integrate renal, hematologic, oncologic, neurologic, burn, sensory, reproductive, immune, infectious, shock, multisystem, and palliative concepts with focused assessment, pharmacology, diagnostics, prioritization, delegation, and communication. The syllabus emphasizes early deterioration recognition, sepsis and shock response, critical-care awareness, complex medication safety, interprofessional coordination, and simulation-based transition-to-practice judgment.',
