us, and hearing loss overview"}, {"id": "c9b084fc-8061-4b34-903f-8a2ab7428c89", "type": "concept", "title": "Fall risk and vestibular symptoms"}, {"id": "14d77b42-9309-4d52-b44e-d500b33d33b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Assistive devices and patient teaching"}]}, {"id": "fb5a9645-0cd4-4e84-a5a0-0b58f944ba8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication safety", "description": "Sensory changes require adaptation in every interaction.", "children": [{"id": "a0cb6aa7-bfdd-4fa8-b6b8-cca265d51a5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible teaching materials"}, {"id": "4c69f262-fca4-484e-9252-873cb1aac90c", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpreter and assistive communication strategies"}, {"id": "06c3e8f7-a439-4dc1-bae5-515df6e3df2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Medication and discharge safety for sensory impairment"}]}]}, {"id": "29ea9448-a068-4412-881c-ab8fd1fc8c60", "type": "topic", "title": "Reproductive, Genitourinary, and Gender-Inclusive Adult Care", "description": "This topic addresses reproductive and genitourinary conditions with attention to dignity, trauma-informed care, and teaching.", "children": [{"id": "0f4fc71e-b3d0-4401-a734-f594359db4a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reproductive assessment", "description": "Students learn respectful, private, trauma-informed assessment.", "children": [{"id": "011b253c-94bd-435e-8e7e-e38affea7f1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sexual and reproductive health history"}, {"id": "6f9fcd6b-dc06-443d-9a96-75e534678f3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Pain, bleeding, discharge, urinary symptoms, and fertility concerns"}, {"id": "76a8722a-2c61-4af8-9cac-b2c8e75f3a50", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and consent"}]}, {"id": "468ee60c-8508-484b-a6a5-7a5db65b45e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common conditions", "description": "This module introduces common adult reproductive and GU issues relevant to med-surg practice.", "children": [{"id": "fa2371e0-0db9-4dda-a9fc-c9fa889fa92c", "type": "concept", "title": "Benign prostatic hyperplasia, prostatitis, and prostate cancer overview"}, {"id": "f8260293-e936-4c3a-9198-e0de77e005bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Gynecologic disorders, pelvic inflammatory disease, and abnormal bleeding"}, {"id": "8a073d5f-c32d-4150-b8c3-9274c0ee0bfb", "type": "concept", "title": "STIs and sexual health teaching"}]}, {"id": "c91f9b85-a7ec-4080-91c8-2d5f9ff3e852", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive nursing care", "description": "Care quality improves when patients' identities, bodies, and goals are respected.", "children": [{"id": "18a8a827-8501-48de-82dd-cb04fa22ef97", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender-inclusive language"}, {"id": "abc4d7bc-3aed-401e-b99d-60452fe1e649", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed pelvic/GU care"}, {"id": "70aaa73d-543e-481d-b7cc-078105f0d7e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening, prevention, and referral resources"}]}]}, {"id": "e9760220-cc6b-4b39-9d8c-8f06ccba72a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Immune, Autoimmune, Infectious Disorders, HIV, and Sepsis", "description": "Students learn care for immune dysfunction, infection, HIV, antimicrobial therapy, isolation, and sepsis escalation.", "children": [{"id": "ff1851ca-a46d-4576-8081-dc97a2a1f281", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Immune dysfunction", "description": "Students learn how altered immunity changes infection risk and nursing priorities.", "children": [{"id": "55edf6ef-0d56-4e3c-a4c5-6c0489170c95", "type": "concept", "title": "Autoimmune disorders and flare patterns"}, {"id": "ce88a87d-c0c9-473c-8b07-0b6fb7125361", "type": "concept", "title": "Immunosuppression and opportunistic infection risk"}, {"id": "f7e02c87-d858-4c9a-bf12-c97d3614faf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Allergic and hypersensitivity responses"}]}, {"id": "621b6065-8dd4-4bbe-9085-fbbfd24d3be5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infectious disease care", "description": "Infections require isolation, antimicrobial stewardship, and patient education.", "children": [{"id": "7cd32031-6368-45dd-